\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \emph  {Paper at a glance.} \textbf  {(A)} Study architecture: four self-computed modalities (scRNA, spatial, scATAC, perturbation) plus an external 12-study meta-analysis are embedded by foundation models \emph  {and} simple baselines, then scored by a fair-evaluation suite (non-linear probe, reference-free structure metrics, split-conformal coverage, an equivalence test, three dose--response analyses). \textbf  {(B)} Argument roadmap: a reference-free re-check turns the two-camp dispute into three findings---the apparent baseline ``win'' dissolves into two artifacts (label circularity, a causal vocabulary threshold), with three dose--response probes (vocabulary coverage, batch-shift strength, spatial-aggregation depth) supplying the mechanisms.}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:schematic}{{1}{3}{\emph {Paper at a glance.} \textbf {(A)} Study architecture: four self-computed modalities (scRNA, spatial, scATAC, perturbation) plus an external 12-study meta-analysis are embedded by foundation models \emph {and} simple baselines, then scored by a fair-evaluation suite (non-linear probe, reference-free structure metrics, split-conformal coverage, an equivalence test, three dose--response analyses). \textbf {(B)} Argument roadmap: a reference-free re-check turns the two-camp dispute into three findings---the apparent baseline ``win'' dissolves into two artifacts (label circularity, a causal vocabulary threshold), with three dose--response probes (vocabulary coverage, batch-shift strength, spatial-aggregation depth) supplying the mechanisms}{figure.1}{}}
