\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces \emph  {The metric-artifact view} (cluster J): two zero-shot FMs (scGPT + Geneformer-V2) vs.\ the best simple baseline across 20 raw-count atlases (3 native + 17 unlocked by barcode label-transfer). \textbf  {(A)} Cross-batch discrimination, scored by a \emph  {linear}-probe AUROC against the labels: the apparent baseline ``win'' is concentrated in the orange \emph  {vocab-mismatch} atlases (8 cross-species mouse-symbol + 1 ENSG-only, where the human-symbol FM tokenizer maps almost no genes); on the 11 blue vocabulary-matched atlases the points hug the diagonal, and the fair re-check (Fig.~\ref {fig:fair}) removes the residual gap as circularity and probe bias. \textbf  {(B)} The matched calibration view (FM ECE vs.\ best-baseline ECE, lower is better): the FMs sit mostly above the diagonal (worse-calibrated out-of-batch), the reliability counterpart that cluster K quantifies and partly repairs.}}{10}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:fmvsbase}{{7}{10}{\emph {The metric-artifact view} (cluster J): two zero-shot FMs (scGPT + Geneformer-V2) vs.\ the best simple baseline across 20 raw-count atlases (3 native + 17 unlocked by barcode label-transfer). \textbf {(A)} Cross-batch discrimination, scored by a \emph {linear}-probe AUROC against the labels: the apparent baseline ``win'' is concentrated in the orange \emph {vocab-mismatch} atlases (8 cross-species mouse-symbol + 1 ENSG-only, where the human-symbol FM tokenizer maps almost no genes); on the 11 blue vocabulary-matched atlases the points hug the diagonal, and the fair re-check (Fig.~\ref {fig:fair}) removes the residual gap as circularity and probe bias. \textbf {(B)} The matched calibration view (FM ECE vs.\ best-baseline ECE, lower is better): the FMs sit mostly above the diagonal (worse-calibrated out-of-batch), the reliability counterpart that cluster K quantifies and partly repairs}{figure.7}{}}
